Theorem RL-1: Realization rule signatures — RL-1 through RL-34 + RL-13 confirmation-of-removal

  Preconditions:
    - Realization rules govern RC emission / COW / reuse / stack promotion /
      header compression / non-atomic RC / KnownSafe + PRE motion / selective
      barriers / LLVM fact export / borrow inference per Annex E §AIMS
    - All RL rules have signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction
      per the canonical proof notation:264
    - 37 active RL theorems (RL-1 through RL-34 minus RL-13-REMOVED, plus
      RL-11a / RL-14a / RL-15a / RL-18a sub-rules) per the section
      inventory table (line 108)
    - RL-13 was REMOVED from Annex E §AIMS (same root cause as DP-10)
    - RL-31 (type-level disjointness) requires cross-call-site
      provenance-summary parameter per Annex E §AIMS RL-31

  Soundness property:
    Common type signature for all RL rules (per the canonical proof notation:264):

      RL-N : ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction

    RC emission cluster (RL-1 through RL-5):
      RL-1 RC inc emission when value duplicated (passed to Owned param
             while still live)
      RL-2 RC dec emission at last use of owned value or scope exit;
             excludes ownership-transferring uses; includes UNUSED-owned
             definitional cleanup for Dead/Absent
      RL-3 RC ops elided when lattice proves unnecessary (via DP-2, DP-3, DP-7)
      RL-4 edge-specific decs on CFG edges with Jump-arg exemption
      RL-5 dead-at-entry cleanup for Owned non-scalar block-params with
             Cardinality = absent

    COW cluster (RL-6 through RL-10):
      RL-6 static unique mutation (Uniqueness = u): in-place, no IsShared
      RL-7 dynamic COW (Uniqueness = ms): IsShared check + branch
      RL-8 static shared mutation (Uniqueness = s): unconditional copy
      RL-9 COW compound contraction (diamond -> single instruction)
      RL-10 disjoint field mutation: NO COW when field-disjoint borrows
             (DP-5 field-aware disjointness; SetTag conservatively blocks)

    Allocation reuse cluster (RL-11 through RL-12, minus RL-13-REMOVED):
      RL-11 same-block reuse: Reset + Reuse pairing per Annex E §AIMS
             RL-11 conditions (a, b, c)
      RL-11a dynamic reuse for MaybeShared: IsShared check; unique fast path,
             shared fresh-allocation slow path
      RL-12 cross-block reuse with dominance / post-dominance + same
             innermost loop header + no-throw constraints

    Stack promotion cluster (RL-14 through RL-16):
      RL-14 non-escaping unique allocations: alloca, no header, no RC,
             field-level RcDec for Owned heap children at scope exit
      RL-14a non-escaping fixed-size non-unique: alloca with MAX_REFCOUNT
             header (immortal); heap children per RL-14
      RL-15 non-escaping dynamic-size: function-local bump allocator;
             bump region freed at function return
      RL-15a ArgEscaping: caller-stack allocation with conservative
             header semantics per callee parameter contract
             (Borrowed+Unique+may_share=false: headerless;
              Borrowed!=Unique: immortal header;
              Owned: immortal header;
              closure capture handled by CN-8 demotion)
      RL-16 escaping (locality >= he): full heap allocation with RC header

    RC header compression cluster (RL-17 through RL-18):
      RL-17 sharing-bound analysis: is_local(s) AND u -> no header;
             straight-line N incs -> Bounded(N+1);
             loops / recursion / global -> Unbounded
      RL-18 header width narrowing per RL-17 result:
             Unique -> none; Bounded <=127 -> i8;
             <=32767 -> i16; <=2^31-1 -> i32; Unbounded -> i64;
             ABI-visible types always full-width

    Unified representation constraint:
      RL-18a all escape-driven decisions consume Locality as primary input;
             thread-boundary analysis is DERIVED, not separate per-variable
             escape dimension

    Non-atomic RC cluster (RL-19 through RL-21):
      RL-19 thread-local values: non-atomic RC (plain load/store)
      RL-20 thread-shared values: atomic RC
      RL-21 no-spawn-no-FFI program: ALL non-atomic

    KnownSafe + PRE-style RC motion cluster (RL-22 through RL-26):
      RL-22 KnownSafe pair elimination when physical RC provably positive
      RL-23 KnownSafe flag propagation at joins (AND across predecessors)
      RL-24 bidirectional dataflow identifies matching (Inc, Dec) pairs
             across blocks
      RL-25 pair eliminable when KnownSafe = true OR both paths safe AND
             no CFG hazard
      RL-26 RC motion forbidden across observable barriers per Annex E §AIMS
             RL-26 (calls to Owned / may_share=true params; IsShared;
              Set / SetTag on aggregate containing v)

    Selective barriers cluster (RL-27 through RL-28):
      RL-27 RC flush at call sites when callee params Owned + non-Dead OR
             Borrowed + may_share=true
      RL-28 unknown callees: conservative flush of all pending RC ops

    AIMS -> LLVM fact export cluster (RL-29 through RL-31):
      RL-29 fresh allocation returns (preserves_freshness=true AND
             uniqueness=u): LLVM noalias marker
      RL-30 effect-based call annotations per IC-3 + IC-5;
             pure calls: memory(none);
             pure read-only: memory(argmem: read);
             allocating + arg-access: memory(argmem: readwrite,
              inaccessiblemem: readwrite);
             deallocating: memory(inaccessiblemem: readwrite);
             fallback: argmem: readwrite + inaccessiblemem: readwrite
      RL-31 disjoint Borrowed parameters: !alias.scope + !noalias metadata
             pairs; cross-call-site provenance-summary parameter required
             (cross-function alias-disjointness proof from borrow_sources +
              project_alias_sources at each call site) — VF-2 (b) consumes
             this; the burden-prototype C5 CRITICAL criterion

    Borrow inference cluster (RL-32 through RL-34):
      RL-32 all non-scalar parameters initialize Borrowed; fixpoint promotes
             to Owned based on demand
      RL-33 projection propagation: projected field Owned -> source promoted
             Owned
      RL-34 tail call preservation: no RcDec after tail call; transfer
             ownership when callee Owned; cannot tail-call Borrowed unless
             dec arranged

    RL-13 confirmation-of-removal entry:

      RL-13 — Construct + Once does NOT imply RC == 1 at death (REMOVED)

      Removed in: Annex E §AIMS RL-13 removal note
        (same root cause as DP-10)

      Root cause: one use may be "store into data structure" (creates alias
        via RcInc); Construct + Cardinality=Once alone does not guarantee
        RC == 1 at death.

      Subsumed by:
        - Uniqueness dimension (§AIMS §3.4) as direct source of truth for
          reuse eligibility
        - DP-6 + RL-11 + RL-12 reuse-candidate gating via Uniqueness

      No theorem skeleton to discharge; this is a CONFIRMATION entry only.

